hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16686","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Imran ibn Abi Anas, from Hanzalah ibn Ali al-Aslami, from Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in Subh while we were with him. When he raised his head from the last rakah, he said: May Allah curse Lihyan, Ril, Dhakwan, and Usayyah; Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive them. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell prostrate. When he finished, he recited to the people and said: O people, I did not say it, but Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said it."
"16687","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Khalid ibn Abdullah ibn Harmalah, from al-Harith ibn Khufaf, from his father Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed in prayer, then raised his head and said: Ghifar, may Allah forgive them, and Aslam, may Allah grant them peace, and Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan. O Allah, curse Ril and Dhakwan. Then he said takbir and fell prostrate. Khufaf said: The cursing of the disbelievers was made because of that."
"16688","He said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Imran ibn Abi Anas, brother of Banu Amir ibn Luayy, and he was trustworthy, narrated to me about the spreading of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of his left thigh in the middle of prayer and at its end, his sitting on his left hip, placing his left hand on his left thigh, erecting his right foot, placing his right hand on his right thigh, and erecting his forefinger, declaring the unity of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with it, from Abu al-Qasim Miqsam, mawla of Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, he said: A man from the people of Madinah narrated to me, he said: I prayed in the mosque of Banu Ghifar, and when I sat in my prayer I spread my left thigh and erected the forefinger. He said: Khufaf ibn Ima ibn Rahdah al-Ghifari saw me, and he had companionship with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while I was doing that. He said: When I finished my prayer, he said to me: O my son, why did you erect your finger thus. He said: What do you object; I saw the people doing that. He said: You did right. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed, used to do that. The polytheists used to say: Muhammad only does this with his finger to bewitch it. They lied. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only did that declaring the unity of his Lord, Mighty and Majestic, with it."
